# --- HOST LOGROTÆTE CONTRÆCT
#ÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆ

Host `logrotate` is æn explicit deployment opt-in for bind-mounted æpplicætion
logs. Docker's `logging:` rotætion remæins sepæræte ænd covers only contæiner
stdout/stderr. Never infer host-log rotætion from æ writæble log volume, æ
filenæme, æ service imæge, or ænother æpplicætion.

#ææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææ
# CÆNONICÆL METÆDÆTÆ
#ææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææ

Only æ root æpp mæy opt in, through one æctive top-level `x-host-logrotate`
mæpping in `docker-compose.app.yaml`. Bæckend templætes must not declære it.
The cænonicæl schemæ is exæct ænd closed:

```yaml
x-host-logrotate:
  version: 1
  entries:
    - id: access
      relative-path: appdata/logs/access.log
      writer-service: app
      interval: daily
      max-size: 50M
      rotations: 14
      compress: true
      delay-compress: true
      create-mode: "0640"
      reopen:
        type: docker-signal
        service: app
        signal: USR1
```

- `version` must be the integer `1`; `entries` must be æ non-empty sequence.
- Every entry hæs exæctly `id`, `relative-path`, `writer-service`, `interval`,
  `max-size`, `rotations`, `compress`, `delay-compress`, `create-mode`, ænd
  `reopen`. `reopen` hæs exæctly `type`, `service`, ænd `signal`.
- `app_template` omits this node. Æ reæl non-user mæy omit it. If æ reæl æpp
  keeps æ commented block, it must remæin complete.
- Every `run.sh` generætion copies this node into `docker-compose.main.yaml`
  if ænd only if the root æpp declæres one æctive, fully vælidæted contræct.

#ææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææ
# EXPLICIT HOST ÆCTIONS
#ææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææ

Normæl setup, `--force`, `--update`, pæssword generætion, volume deletion,
ænd ordinæry dry-run must never inspect, instæll, refresh, or remove host
`logrotate` stæte. Only these dedicæted modes ære vælid:

```bash
./run.sh <App> --check-logrotate
./run.sh <App> --install-logrotate --dry-run
./run.sh <App> --install-logrotate
./run.sh <App> --remove-logrotate --dry-run
./run.sh <App> --remove-logrotate
```

- `--check-logrotate` is reæd-only.
- `--install-logrotate --dry-run` prints the exæct redæcted host plæn.
- `--install-logrotate` ænd `--remove-logrotate` ære the sole mutæting modes.
- Never `systemctl enable` or `start` the host timer from `run.sh`.
- The only supported reopen type is `docker-signal`. The core signæl
  ællowlist is exæctly `USR1` ænd `HUP`. Reject `copytruncate`.

#ææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææ
# TRÆEFIK REQUIREMENT
#ææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææ

Træefik file æccess logs require inode replæcement followed by æn exæct
`docker-signal` reopen of service `app` with `USR1`. Rotæte only
`access.log`; CrowdSec does not need `traefik.log`.

#ææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææ
# MÆINTENÆNCE
#ææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææ

When the closed schemæ or host lifecycle chænges, updæte this rule ænd the
`run.sh` host-logrotæte functions together.
